# License

## Status: To Be Determined

The AISESA AI Working Group is evaluating licensing options for this toolkit to ensure maximum accessibility while preserving attribution and maintaining African ownership.

## Candidate Licenses Under Consideration:

### Option 1: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
**Allows**:
- Sharing, copying, redistribution
- Adaptation, remixing, building upon

**Requirements**:
- Attribution to AISESA AI Working Group
- Link to license
- Indication if changes were made

**Best for**: Maximum openness and reuse

**License text**: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

---

### Option 2: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0)
**Allows**:
- Sharing, copying, redistribution
- Adaptation, remixing, building upon

**Requirements**:
- Attribution to AISESA AI Working Group
- Link to license
- Indication if changes were made
- **Derivatives must use the same license** (copyleft provision)

**Best for**: Ensuring adaptations remain open and accessible

**License text**: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

---

## Decision Timeline

The working group will select a license by **Q1 2026**, after consultation with:
- AISESA member organizations
- Legal advisors familiar with African IP frameworks
- Community feedback

## Questions or Input?

If you have expertise in open licensing or perspectives on which license best serves African AI governance goals, please share via [GitHub Discussions](../../discussions) or contact the working group chair.

---

**Temporary Status**: Until a license is formally adopted, materials in this repository are:
- Shared for working group collaboration and development
- Not for commercial redistribution without permission
- Subject to AISESA organizational policies

---

**Last Updated**: November 2025
